## D. FINDINGS FIXED IN THIS BATCH
1. capacity: each open stream waits on its provider in a worker thread; on the shared default pool many streams would
   starve plain calls, the catalog and key lookups. Now a dedicated pool of 16 per process, 503 + Retry-After when full,
   before any provider is called.
2. a key lookup failing inside the worker thread mid-call would have been recorded as client_disconnected; now gateway_error.
3. the record task of the final "done" step is kept alive (strong ref) if the client leaves at that moment.

## E. NOT PROVEN
no live provider stream (or any live call); stream_options.include_usage on real providers (mistral excluded on documentation
belief, not verified); that real providers stop generating when the connection closes; no production record; no UI.
A cancel is seen at the provider's next line (or the 60 s read timeout), not instantly.

